## Localization

Three loc keys per move, in any `.yml` file under
`localization/english/`. The file must start with a UTF-8 BOM followed
by the `l_english:` header line.

```yaml
l_english:
 POD_combat_move_<skill_key>:0 "Display Name"
 POD_combat_move_<skill_key>_desc:0 "[PODCombatMoveDesc('POD_combat_move_<skill_key>')]"
 POD_combat_move_<skill_key>_tooltip:0 "#weak;italic <flavor sentence>#!"
```

| Key | What it is |
|---|---|
| `POD_combat_move_<skill_key>` | The short display name, shown in the loadout editor and on the move button. The AP cost is appended automatically at render, so do not write it into the name. |
| `..._desc` | The decision description. CK3 auto-resolves `<decision_id>_desc`; the `PODCombatMoveDesc` macro reads the move's runtime story variables and renders the full stat card (costs, damage, flags). **Always use the macro form exactly as shown** - any custom prose here replaces the dynamic stat block. |
| `..._tooltip` | A short flavor sentence (styled `#weak;italic ...#!`) rendered as the italic flavor line on the move's tooltip card. CK3's automatic `<decision_id>_tooltip` lookup does **not** fire for hidden decisions; this key is reached through the `PODCombatMoveFlavor` data-binding macro, which builds it from the move's `skill_key`. Leave it `""` for no flavor line. |

`gui/POD_combat_l_english.yml` holds the bulk per-move catalogue keys;
`gui/POD_combat_static_l_english.yml` is the shared static loc. Either
works - put your three keys in the static file to keep your hand-added
moves grouped and out of the bulk catalogue file.

