## Picking values

Numbers come from the `@`-constant families at the top of
`pod_combat_move_list_effects.txt` (full table in **Constants
reference**). Raw integers work too, but constants make a global
rebalance one edit. These tables are starting points - read the actual
constant values before committing.

### AP cost

A turn is 6 AP. The AP cost decides how many moves fit in a turn.

| AP | Role | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| 1-2 | Light / chainable | Cheap jabs, AP cantrips, quick stances. |
| 3 | Standard | Bread-and-butter attacks, most discipline taps. Two fit in a turn. |
| 4 | Bigger swing | Heavy attacks, mid-tier disciplines. |
| 5 | Heavy | Reckless charges, strong combat-long buffs. |
| 6 | Whole-turn signature | AoE disciplines, ultimates. |

Do not make everything 6 AP - that flattens the tactical choice of
mixing cheap and expensive moves in a turn.

### Energy cost

Energy is the actor's splat pool (blood / gnosis / pathos / glamour /
resolve / ...), resolved at runtime.

| Energy | Use for |
|---|---|
| 2 | Most discipline moves at base level. |
| 4 | Advanced or signature discipline uses. |

### HP damage

Wound tracks are roughly 5-7 boxes, so a 5-damage hit can drop a tough
character in one landed swing. Ladder damage no faster than you ladder
cost.

| Damage | Use for |
|---|---|
| 1 | Light / cheap moves. |
| 2 | Standard attacks and most disciplines. |
| 3 | Bigger gifts, weapon strikes with an elemental damage class. |
| 4 | Heavy / signature. |
| 5+ | Exceptional; the AP and energy cost should match. |

### Morale damage

Morale max is 20, and morale sources are plentiful, so keep these below
HP-damage values. Standard range is 1-3, 4+ for signature mental
attacks. The target's end-of-combat morale deficit converts to Mental
Strain once, multiplied by `pod_combat_morale_stress_multiplier` (5).

### AI weight

`AI_WEIGHT` is the move's base selection weight. The defaults track the
move's category:

| Category | Default `AI_WEIGHT` |
|---|---|
| ATK | 20 |
| PWR | 12 |
| CTL | 10 |
| DEF | 8 |

Any other or unmapped category defaults to 5. Follow these so the AI
behaves predictably. Override only when a move is unusually strong or
weak for its category (e.g. a 6-AP signature might warrant 20 so the AI
actually reaches for it). Note that non-starter (gated) moves already
get a separate class-repertoire bonus from the AI selector
(`@ai_trait_gated`, +18) on top of `AI_WEIGHT`.

### Tier magnitudes

Buff/debuff tiers are fixed at TIER 1 / 2 / 3 = +/-10 / +/-20 / +/-30.
Combat-duration tiers are stronger than round-duration because they
persist all fight, so price them higher. Round-duration tiers clear at
the holder's next turn (a soak buff still covers the intervening enemy
phase), so they cost less and don't snowball.

### Self-damage

Pair self-damage with high HP damage - the trade is "bigger hit, you
take some back." The canonical pattern is a reckless charge: high damage
to the target plus 1 self-damage at 6 AP. Self-damage is always
superficial, soakable, and ignores stances.

