## Checklist & smoke test

### Before testing

- [ ] Hidden decision name matches the constructor's `DECISION` exactly.
- [ ] `SKILL_KEY` matches the decision suffix (decision
  `POD_combat_move_foo` -> `SKILL_KEY = foo`).
- [ ] All three loc keys exist: `<key>`, `<key>_desc`, `<key>_tooltip`.
- [ ] `_desc` uses the macro
  `[PODCombatMoveDesc('POD_combat_move_<key>')]` and nothing else.
- [ ] The loc file starts with a UTF-8 BOM and `l_english:` header.
- [ ] All seven constructor parameters are set.
- [ ] The move actually does something: HP damage -> `hp_damage`,
  healing -> `hp_heal` with `TYPE`, buff -> a tier setter, stance -> a
  flag. A move with no setters loads but does nothing when fired.
- [ ] `team_enemy` / `team_ally` AoE moves size `hp_damage` per-enemy,
  not summed.
- [ ] If `retaliate_damage` is set, the matching `retaliate_if_hit` /
  `retaliate_if_missed` flag is also set.
- [ ] Supernatural (auto-hit) moves carry `checks_stance` only - no
  `requires_hit_roll`, no `checks_guard`.
- [ ] **Gating:** a move with no unlock-dispatcher branch is
  runtime-*ungated* - anyone can equip it and every NPC AI gets it. If
  it must be restricted, add a `flag:<skill_key>` branch to the
  dispatcher and mirror the check in the decision; if it is meant to be
  universal, set the decision gate to `always = yes` so the display
  matches. See **Unlock gating**.

### In-game smoke test

1. Load a save with a character whose traits/perks satisfy the gate.
2. Open **Configure Combat Skills**. The move should appear in the right
   column under its `CONFIG` section header.
3. Equip it - the left-side card updates.
4. Start a debug combat. The move appears in the action bar.
5. Click it. The expected effects fire (damage rolls, heal applies, buff
   stacks).
6. Check the combat log for the resolution line.

### If something is wrong

- **Move doesn't appear:** check the error log for unresolved decisions
  or loc keys; confirm the registration effect is wired into game start;
  temporarily swap the gate to `always = yes` to rule out the gate
  excluding your test character.
- **Tooltip looks wrong:** the `_desc` must call `PODCombatMoveDesc` and
  nothing else; reload the game so the macro reads a freshly built
  catalogue (a move registered late won't render until the catalogue
  rebuilds).
- **Anyone can equip it, or every NPC uses it:** the move has no
  unlock-dispatcher branch, so it falls through to *always unlocked*.
  Restrict it by adding a `flag:<skill_key>` branch to the dispatcher
  and mirroring the check in the decision. See **Unlock gating**.
- **Move appears on a fresh game but not an existing save:** bump
  `POD_current_combat_version` in `pod_combat_values.txt`. The
  configure-skills decision rebuilds the catalogue when the save's
  stored version differs, and that rebuild is what picks up a newly
  added move.

