## Constants reference

All numeric constants are declared at the top of
`pod_combat_move_list_effects.txt`. Editing one rebalances every move
that references it, so prefer constants over raw integers. Outliers that
fit no tier print as raw integers; both forms work identically.

| Family | Values |
|---|---|
| `@ap_cost_*` | `tiny=1`, `minor=2`, `medium=3`, `major=4`, `massive=5`, `maximum=6` |
| `@energy_cost_*` | `tiny=1`, `minor=2`, `medium=3`, `major=4`, `massive=5`, `maximum=6` |
| `@stress_cost_*` | `minor=10`, `medium=20`, `major=40`, `massive=80` |
| `@gold_cost_*` | `minor=15`, `medium=50`, `major=150`, `massive=500` |
| `@piety_cost_*` | `minor=50`, `medium=100`, `major=250`, `massive=500` |
| `@prestige_cost_*` | `minor=50`, `medium=100`, `major=250`, `massive=500` |
| `@damage_*` | `tiny=1`, `minor=2`, `medium=3`, `major=4`, `massive=5`, `maximum=6` |
| `@morale_damage_*` | `tiny=1`, `minor=2`, `medium=3`, `major=4`, `massive=5`, `maximum=6` |
| `@self_damage_*` | `tiny=1`, `minor=2`, `medium=3` |
| `@healing_*` | `tiny=1`, `minor=2`, `medium=3`, `major=4`, `massive=5` |
| `@morale_heal_*` | `tiny=1`, `minor=2`, `medium=3`, `major=4`, `massive=5` |

Texture constants are declared at the top of
`pod_combat_move_decisions.txt`. The four category fallbacks:

| Constant | Image file | Use for |
|---|---|---|
| `@texture_atk` | `decision_bloodsurge.dds` | ATK moves |
| `@texture_def` | `decision_warding_evil.dds` | DEF moves |
| `@texture_ctl` | `decision_eye_of_the_storm.dds` | CTL moves |
| `@texture_pwr` | `decision_blood_moon.dds` | PWR moves |

Alongside them is a per-discipline / power-family family
(`@texture_celerity`, `@texture_serpentis`, `@texture_dominate`,
`@texture_obfuscate`, `@texture_bloodsorcery`, `@texture_demonology`,
`@texture_theurgy`, ...) pointing at each discipline's
`decision_POD_<name>.dds`, plus `@texture_faith` for covenant moves.
Prefer a family texture when the move belongs to a named discipline.
